From a91ca7b19c2b7eeb1746846d4a9c768e7ea27188 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "gastown.slit (polecat)" <polecat-gastown.slit@soundit.local>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 23:45:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add billing calendar for upcoming invoice dates
 (psa-g9l)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a Billing Calendar page (GitHub #102) that forecasts when recurring
invoices are due to be generated. There was previously no calendar or
upcoming-invoices view — next_run_date was only visible per-profile on the
recurring profiles list.

What it does:
- New /billing/calendar page (billing.calendar) with a sidebar link under
  Billing, and a 3/6/12/24-month horizon selector.
- Projects each active profile's next_run_date forward by its billing period
  (mirroring BillingService::advanceNextRunDate) to build a real multi-month
  schedule, grouped by calendar month with per-month counts and estimated
  totals, plus summary tiles.
- Surfaces an "Overdue" bucket for profiles whose next_run_date is already
  past and awaiting generation (exactly one pending row per profile).
- Estimated amounts reuse BillingService::previewInvoice (computed once per
  profile — the subtotal is date-independent) and are clearly labelled as
  estimates based on current quantities.

Design notes:
- Only active profiles on active, PSA-billed contracts are included, reusing
  Contract::active()/psaManaged() scopes (mirrors RecurringInvoiceProfile
  scopeDue minus the due-date filter).
- Logic lives in a dedicated BillingCalendarService (thin controller per house
  style); the projection loop is bounded to guard against runaway iteration on
  badly-overdue monthly profiles.
- next_run_date is a date-only field, so no timezone conversion is applied
  (consistent with the recurring profiles list).

Validation: 11 new feature/service tests (empty/future/overdue rendering,
active-only + PSA-only filtering, auth, monthly/quarterly projection counts,
horizon scaling, estimate totals). Full suite green (2579 passed), Pint clean
on changed files.
